{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#929","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#929","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#929\",\"parent_revision\":\"67c3ba1768fbc4ff3aa8dc8a864f4875ae0408d3\",\"root_revision\":\"29dd0bf83aea0c172d060dda65e9041c2e010cf846ec9cbd758b0b0c4e407ca1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd a PostToolUseFailure hook that tracks consecutive tool failures. After 3 failures: inject try a different approach guidance. After 5 lifetime trips: escalate to stop and rethink. Catches agent failure loops that our blocker reporting misses. Pattern sourced from Citadel circuit-breaker.js.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-19T13:36:34.315403Z</sub>\\n\\nREPRO-2956-WRITEPATH-FC-20260819-b7c201\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-19T13:35:41.809461Z</sub>\\n\\nREPRO-2956-WRITEPATH-RTICA-20260819-b7c201\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-19T13:37:24.028230Z</sub>\\n\\nREPRO-2956-WRITEPATH-IC-20260819-b7c201\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **circuit breaker hook for agent failure loops** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Citadel assessment .claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Working Register\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-19T13:34:48.716753Z</sub>\\n\\nREPRO-2956-WRITEPATH-WR-20260819-b7c201\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Agent failure loops are a real failure mode (documented in investigation escalation anti-pattern). Without circuit breaking, a stuck agent can consume the session budget silently. Existing hooks address delegation discipline but not runtime failure loops.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: sessions where an agent retries the same failing tool call repeatedly without human visibility\\n- Bottleneck: no current hook intercepts repeated tool failures; the only mitigation is the blocker reporting in CLAUDE.md, which requires the agent to self-report\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Surfaces failure loops that blocker reporting misses (agent may not self-report if it believes a retry will succeed)\\n- Injects course-correction guidance at exactly 3 failures before context budget is wasted\\n- Escalates to hard stop at 5 lifetime trips to prevent session-budget exhaustion\\n- Complements existing PreToolUse orchestrator-discipline hooks with a runtime failure dimension\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a tool fails N times consecutively within a session, the hook injects guidance into Claude's context at threshold 3 (soft: try a different approach) and terminates Claude's turn at threshold 5 (hard: stop and rethink). Between failures, the counter resets on any successful tool call. State is persisted to a per-session file so it survives context compaction within the session.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA PostToolUseFailure hook script (`.cjs`, Node.js per language conventions) registered in `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/hooks.json`. A per-session failure state file at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/circuit-breaker-{session_id}.json` tracks consecutive failure count and lifetime trip count per tool (or globally). The hook reads this file, increments counters, writes it back, then returns the appropriate JSON output.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After 3 consecutive failures of any tool in a session, the hook injects `additionalContext` text containing \\\"try a different approach\\\" into Claude's context.\\n2. After 5 lifetime trips (threshold crossings) in the same session, the hook sets `continue: false` with a stop reason directing Claude to stop and rethink.\\n3. A successful tool call between failures resets the consecutive failure counter to 0 (requires a companion PostToolUse handler or state file check).\\n4. State file exists at `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/circuit-breaker-{session_id}.json` after a session with at least one PostToolUseFailure event.\\n5. The hook exits 0 silently when below the threshold (no output injected).\\n6. The hook skips processing in kage-bunshin child sessions (`KAGE_BUNSHIN_CHILD=1`) to avoid cross-session interference, matching the pattern in `stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs`.\\n7. `hooks.json` for orchestrator-discipline plugin registers the new hook under `PostToolUseFailure`.\\n\\n### Human Input\\n\\nThe item description references \\\"Citadel circuit-breaker.js\\\" from `.claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md`. That file was not found in the working tree (no `.claude/reports/` directory exists). The Citadel pattern (3-failure soft inject, 5-lifetime hard stop) is sourced from that assessment and is treated as the intended design. Human should confirm:\\n- Whether the counters are per-tool-name or global across all tools\\n- Whether \\\"lifetime\\\" means per-session or persisted across sessions\\n- Whether the hard stop at 5 should set `continue: false` (halts the turn) or exit 2 (blocks tool and feeds message to Claude)\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the failure counter be tracked per tool name (e.g., 3 consecutive Bash failures) or globally (3 failures of any tool in a row)?\\n- Does \\\"lifetime trips\\\" mean within a single session, or persisted across sessions in the project state directory?\\n- For the hard stop at 5 trips: `continue: false` halts Claude's response; exit code 2 feeds stderr back to Claude without halting. Which is intended?\\n- Should the consecutive counter reset on any successful tool call, or only on a successful call of the same tool type that was failing?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-core-reference |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-io-api |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:hooks-patterns |\\n| Prior work | plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/pre-tool-diagnostic-command-gate.cjs |\\n| Prior work | plugins/development-harness/hooks/stop-kage-bunshin-idle-check.cjs |\\n| Prior work | plugins/orchestrator-discipline/.claude-plugin/plugin.json |\\n| Prior work | plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/ (no hooks.json yet \u2014 plugin.json references ./hooks.json which is missing) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (standalone hook)\\n- Blocks: #1109 Behavioral fingerprint tracking in PostToolUse hook \u2014 both hooks write state files to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/`; the circuit breaker may want to reuse the telemetry JSONL infrastructure once #1109 is implemented\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- `PostToolUseFailure` input schema for the `Agent` tool is not confirmed in hooks-io-api SKILL.md. The schema shows `tool_name` and `tool_input` fields for leaf tools (Bash, Write, Edit, Read) but does not explicitly document what `tool_input` looks like when `tool_name` is `Agent`. Needs verification before implementing the matcher.\\n- Citadel reference file `.claude/reports/citadel-assessment-20260320.md` not found in working tree \u2014 cannot verify the exact thresholds (3/5) or the Citadel-specific state model\\n- `plugins/orchestrator-discipline/hooks/hooks.json` does not exist (plugin.json references `./hooks.json` but the file is absent). Creating it is part of the implementation scope.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 1 new `.cjs` hook file (~100 lines), 1 new `hooks.json` for the plugin, and a state file schema. Pattern is well-established by existing hooks in the same plugin and in development-harness.\\n\",\"digest\":\"16b94dd8f1fd93da097ad6e4b57e4b279e41c0e3f5c461aa8d9cfe6030f3e661\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnanEA\"}"}